<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ValidationRule xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, NOT IN <description>, AND IT MUST STAY THAT WAY.
        ValidationRule.Description is capped at 255 characters. The full rationale below is
        operationally important, so it was moved here rather than trimmed; a comment is
        repo-only and is never sent to the Metadata API, so it can be as long as it needs to
        be. Do not paste this back into <description>.

        REPLACES NDA_Signed_Before_Underwriting (2026-08-04, destructive rename, see
        manifest/stage-validations). Widened from a single Underwriting-entry gate to a
        5-stage gate covering Underwriting, LOI, Under Contract (PSA), About to Close AND
        Closed Won, closing
        the shortcut hole where a deal could reach Closed Won via About to Close with an
        unsigned NDA. A future stage added to the pipeline must be added to this OR list
        explicitly, it is not covered automatically.

        PHASE 2 (2026-08-14): the third gated stage was renamed 'PSA' ->
        'Under Contract (PSA)'. Only the value moved; the stage list is otherwise unchanged.
        MIGRATION SAFETY - MEASURED FROM THIS FORMULA, NOT ASSUMED: the P2 backfill runs
        BETWEEN P2-D1 and P2-D2, while this OR list still names 'PSA'. It writes the NEW
        value, which matches no entry in the list, so the OR is false and this rule cannot
        fire on the backfill. Repointing this file BEFORE the backfill would break it.

        Gate applies to the stage transition only (ISCHANGED), so approval-process
        rejections and existing records already sitting in a gated stage are unaffected
        (known-open insert-time hole, accepted, see ARCHITECTURE.md discussion of this
        change).
    -->
    <fullName>NDA_Signed_Before_Deal_Progression</fullName>
    <active>true</active>
    <description>Blocks stage entry to Underwriting, LOI, Under Contract (PSA), About to Close, or Closed Won unless the primary NDA is signed. See the XML comment in this file.</description>
    <errorConditionFormula>AND(
    ISCHANGED(StageName),
    OR(
        ISPICKVAL(StageName, &apos;Underwriting&apos;),
        ISPICKVAL(StageName, &apos;LOI&apos;),
        ISPICKVAL(StageName, &apos;Under Contract (PSA)&apos;),
        ISPICKVAL(StageName, &apos;About to Close&apos;),
        ISPICKVAL(StageName, &apos;Closed Won&apos;)
    ),
    OR(
        ISBLANK(Primary_NDA__c),
        NOT(Primary_NDA__r.NDA_Signed__c)
    )
)</errorConditionFormula>
    <errorDisplayField>StageName</errorDisplayField>
    <errorMessage>The primary NDA must be signed before this deal can move to this stage. Link a signed NDA (Primary NDA) first.</errorMessage>
</ValidationRule>
